# ── Foundry .gitignore ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Reorganised 2026-08-18. It had grown by appending, so `node_modules/`, `dist/`,
# `.DS_Store` and `.env` each appeared TWICE and `plans/` appeared as a
# commented-out rule on line 12 and a live one on line 80 — which reads, on a
# skim, as though plans were tracked. Nothing was removed from what is ignored;
# the duplicates were merged and every load-bearing comment was kept verbatim,
# because each one records a decision rather than a preference.
#
# ⚠ Two rules here are LOAD-BEARING and are explained where they sit rather than
# here: the `.env.local.example` exemption, and `/plans`. Read those comments
# before touching either.

# ── Dependencies and build output ────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
ux-flow/
dist/
build/
.next/
.next-verify/
.vite/
.turbo/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Tool caches. Re-created on demand and worth nobody's diff.
.eslintcache
.parcel-cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# Extension catalog cache (re-fetched on demand)
.specify/extensions/.cache/

# ── Lockfiles: pnpm is the ONLY one ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ `package-lock.json` was TRACKED until 2026-08-18 and was a 250-byte stub —
# one empty root entry, no dependencies, and `"engines": {"node": ">=20"}` while
# both real `package.json`s say `>=22`. `packageManager` pins `pnpm@10.29.2`, so
# the file could only ever mislead: `npm install` against it installs nothing,
# and its engine floor contradicted the one the test suite actually needs (the
# Node 20 jsdom failure is exactly what that disagreement costs). Deleted, and
# ignored here so a stray `npm install` cannot quietly reintroduce it.
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ── Secrets — NEVER commit ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Local values live in .env; document variable NAMES as placeholders in
# .env.example (which IS committed).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template
# ⚠ `.env.local.example` is a PLACEHOLDER file and belongs in the repo, exactly
# as the comment above says of `.env.example`. Without this line `.env.*` swallows
# it: `packages/client/.env.local.example` documents the four Entra SSO variable
# names and nothing else records them, so restoring the file after `3e0dd30`
# deleted it would silently leave it untracked and one `git clean` from gone
# again. The real secret file, `.env.local`, is still ignored by `.env.*` — only
# the `*.example` spelling is exempted here.
!.env.local.example
!**/.env.local.example

# ⚠ Timestamped hand-backups of an env file — `.env.bak-1786962128`,
# `.env.local.bak-1787032496`. `.env.*` already catches the repo-root spelling,
# but not a nested one or a `.bak` of a differently-named file, and these hold
# LIVE credentials: API keys, the JWT signing secret, the Entra client secret.
# Ignored explicitly so a copy made while debugging cannot be committed by a
# `git add -A` on the day it is made. ⚠ Ignoring is not deleting — a stale
# `.env.bak-*` is still a plaintext credential on disk. Delete them when done.
*.bak
*.bak-*
.env.bak*
**/.env.local.bak*

# Keys, certificates and credential files, by extension and by conventional name.
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.ppk
id_rsa*
id_dsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
.netrc
.pypirc
credentials.json
*-credentials.json
service-account*.json
terraform.tfstate
terraform.tfstate.*

# ⚠ Backup artifacts contain SCRAM role password hashes (scripts/backup.sh), and
# `roles.sql` inside them is cluster state no per-database dump carries. The
# artifact directory is created 0700 and the file 0600; this keeps it out of git
# as the second layer.
backups/

# ── Working-tree-only: per-developer and per-feature state ───────────────────
#
# Per-developer local feature pointer written by spec-kit commands.
# Never commit: two developers on different features would conflict on every merge.
.specify/feature.json

# Per-developer agent settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# Spec-kit feature artifacts (spec.md/plan.md/tasks.md/etc.) — working-tree-only,
# same convention the krt/guardrail_validation branch used. Keeps every
# developer's in-progress feature directories out of history and off every
# other branch's diff; the reasoning that matters long-term belongs in docs/.
# specs/

# ⚠ `/plans` IS THE KNOWN EXPOSURE, not an oversight. The current plan
# (`plans/foundations-2026-08-10/`) was moved out of `docs/programmes/` on
# 2026-08-11 at the user's instruction and left untracked, so **edits to it are
# not in git** — stated before the move and accepted. `docs/` is the durable
# home; `docs/programmes/README.md` carries the fuller note, including the
# argument the move went against, kept verbatim because it was overruled rather
# than withdrawn. Its last committed state is `cd4387c`.
#
# ⚠ There used to be a commented-out `# plans/` near the top of this file as
# well. A rule that is present-but-disabled beside a live one that does the same
# thing is how somebody concludes the opposite of what is true; the live rule is
# here and there is now only one.
/plans
# A local archive of what is now docs/programmes/ — redundant, and must never be committed.
plan.zip

# ── Editor and OS junk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
*.orig
*.rej

# ── Docs: planning notes are local, REFERENCE docs stay in git ────────────────
#
# ⚠ **`docs/` IS NOT IGNORED WHOLESALE, and the split is the whole point.** Asked
# for on 2026-08-18 as "docs needs to go into gitignore"; scoped to the planning
# half after the cost of the other reading was put on the table and the narrower
# one chosen. What that reading would have cost: 27 `docs/…` citations in
# CLAUDE.md and 92 in code, scripts and CI pointing at paths a fresh clone would
# not have, `ci/spec-policy.sh`'s `docs/*) return 0` exemption and
# `check-spec-compliance.sh`'s "docs-only change → PASS" becoming dead code, and
# `docs/kestra-migration/`'s pinned design — 22 files implementation is forbidden
# to edit — leaving the repo.
#
# ⚠ Adding a directory here does NOT untrack what is already in it. These four
# were untracked with `git rm -r --cached` in the same commit; **their last
# tracked state is `c157947`**:
#
#     git show c157947:docs/programmes/README.md          # read one file
#     git checkout c157947 -- docs/programmes/            # restore it all
#
# ⚠ **THE EXPOSURE THIS CREATES IS THE ONE `plans/` ALREADY CARRIES, and it has
# bitten this repo before.** `docs/programmes/` was RESTORED to `docs/` on
# 2026-08-10 precisely because records kept only in a gitignored directory were
# one `rm` from gone — which had already happened to them once. From this commit
# on, edits to these four are not in git. That is recorded here rather than left
# to be discovered, exactly as the `/plans` note above does it.
#
# ⚠ `docs/programmes/README.md` is the sharpest case: CLAUDE.md states it is
# "now the only copy of that reasoning in the working tree" — the load-bearing
# summaries of three programmes whose full records were already deleted. Losing
# the working-tree copy now means recovering it from history or not at all.
docs/programmes/
docs/intent/
docs/ui-mock/
docs/validation-and-guardrails-roadmap.md

# Design workshop scratch: generated mockups are approval artifacts, not source.
# Only the mockups/ subtree is ignored so docs/design/README.md stays tracked.
docs/design/mockups/

# ⚠ STAYS TRACKED, deliberately — do not add these:
#   docs/kestra-migration/  the pinned design (02-rules.md's R1–R9 and the
#                           worked example); implementation does not edit it
#   docs/GAPS.md            every known gap with its OPEN/DELIBERATE/CLOSED
#                           evidence; several entries are decisions, not bugs
#   docs/STANDARDS.md       · docs/TEAM-WORKFLOW.md · docs/design/README.md

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log

# ⚠ NOT ignored, deliberately: `drizzle/meta/_journal.json`. Its `.bak` is junk,
# but the journal itself is the migration watermark's source of truth — a rewrite
# of one entry's `when` is what made `0033` re-run for ever (see CLAUDE.md's
# migrations note). It must stay in git so that rewrite is visible in a diff.
drizzle/meta/_journal.json.bak

# ── Corporate CA staged for Docker builds (feature 20260824-211547-docker-ca-trust)
#
# `infra/certs/` holds the corporate root certificate staged by
# scripts/stage-corp-ca.sh so that image builds behind a TLS-intercepting proxy
# can trust it. The material is PUBLIC (a CA's public certificate is not a
# secret) but it is organisation-specific, and Constitution VIII prohibits
# committing key material regardless of sensitivity.
#
# ⚠ THE STAGED FILE MUST BE `*.pem`, NEVER `*.crt`. The rule at the top of this
# section's neighbour (`*.pem`, line ~87) covers `.pem` and there is NO `*.crt`
# rule anywhere in this file — so a file staged as `corp-ca.crt` would be
# untracked by intent but not by rule. Where a `.crt` extension is required
# (Debian's /usr/local/share/ca-certificates only processes *.crt), the rename
# happens inside the Dockerfile's COPY, not here.
#
# ⚠ `.gitkeep` is deliberately NOT ignored. The directory must exist in a fresh
# clone or `COPY certs/ …` fails the build. The ignore rule and the tracked
# placeholder are a pair; removing either makes a clean checkout unbuildable.
infra/certs/*
!infra/certs/.gitkeep

# macOS resource-fork shadow dir from unzipping ux-flow/
__MACOSX/
ux-flow.zip
.harness-results/

# Pi builder isolated sandboxes (per-session, local only)
packages/server/.pi-sandboxes/

# Local output folder (not part of the repo)
/packages/Finaloutput/
